---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, isCommodityNode } from '../lib/site-variant';

if (!isCommodityNode) return Astro.redirect('/blog/');
const canonicalUrl = absoluteUrl('/editorial-policy/');
---

<Base
  title="Editorial policy"
  metaTitle="Editorial Policy | CommodityNode"
  description="CommodityNode publication, sourcing, review, conflicts, AI-assistance, and correction standards."
  canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
>
  <article class="static-page prose">
    <p class="section-label">Editorial standards</p>
    <h1>Evidence before narrative.</h1>
    <p class="article-dek">
      CommodityNode publishes commodity-impact research only when the claim type, source trail,
      timestamps, units, uncertainty, and reviewer are visible.
    </p>

    <h2>What counts as a publishable fact</h2>
    <p>
      A verified fact must be directly supported by a named source. A reported claim remains
      attributed to the party making it. Calculated metrics identify their inputs and method.
      Analyst inferences and scenarios are labeled and are never presented as observed facts.
    </p>

    <h2>Source threshold</h2>
    <p>
      Material and critical Event Pulse records require an authoritative primary source or at
      least two independently useful sources. Exact event date and location, affected entities,
      known contradictions, and unsupported capacity figures are checked before publication.
    </p>

    <h2>AI assistance</h2>
    <p>
      Automation may help classify records, identify entities, compare revisions, or prepare a
      draft. It cannot supply missing evidence, invent a number, approve its own output, or create
      an undisclosed byline. A human reviewer remains responsible for published analysis.
    </p>

    <h2>Independence and conflicts</h2>
    <p>
      Advertising, sponsorship, affiliate relationships, or product access do not determine a
      conclusion. Material financial or commercial conflicts must be disclosed with the affected
      article. Sponsored material, if introduced, will be labeled before the title and excluded
      from editorial scoring.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections and expiry</h2>
    <p>
      New evidence may revise or invalidate an edge, event, or conclusion. Material changes keep
      their earlier state in the audit record and publish a correction note. Read the
      <a href="/corrections/"> corrections policy</a> for severity and response rules.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
